where we exclude terms associated with vertex renormalization that are not needed to this order in perturbation theory. Specifically, we have

$$ \Pi_{\sigma}(J)=-g\hskip 0.5pt\hskip 0.5ptG^{\varphi}(1)-\tfrac{1}{2}g_{\sigma}\hskip 0.5ptG^{\sigma}(1)-J(J+2\alpha)\delta_{Z_{\sigma}}\!-\delta_{m_{\sigma}}\,, $$

where $G(1)\equiv\lim_{\xi\to 1}G(\xi)\equiv\lim_{y\to x}G(x,y)$ represents the coincident limit of the propagator. These diagrams are UV divergent and, as before, we regularize them via dimensional regularization by working in $\alpha=\tfrac{1}{2}(3-\epsilon)$ and taking $\epsilon\to 0$ with masses held fixed. We define the coincident limit of the free-field propagator in general dimensions as

$$ \displaystyle G(1) \displaystyle=\frac{1}{(4\pi)^{\alpha+\frac{1}{2}}}\,\Gamma\!\left[\genfrac{.}{.}{-1.0pt}{0}{\raisebox{-1pt}{$\frac{1}{2} - \alpha\,,\, \Delta\,,\, 2\alpha- \Delta$}}{\raisebox{1pt}{$\frac{1}{2} +\alpha- \Delta\,,\, \frac{1}{2} -\alpha+ \Delta$}}\right] $$

which, as $\epsilon\to 0$ , behaves as

$$ G(1)\sim-\frac{(\Delta-1)(\bar{\Delta}-1)}{16\pi^{2}}\left[\frac{2}{\epsilon}-\psi\big(\Delta-1\big)-\psi\big(\bar{\Delta}-1\big)+\log 4\pi{{\mathrm{e}}}^{{\scalebox{0.6}[0.85]{$-$}}\gamma_{\textsc{e}}}+1\right]-\frac{1}{8\pi^{2}}\,, $$

with $\gamma_{\textsc{e}}\equiv-\psi(1)$ the Euler-Mascheroni constant and $\psi(z)=\Gamma^{\prime}(z)/\Gamma(z)$ the digamma function. In our renormalization scheme, this contribution is completely absorbed by the mass counterterm, such that $\delta_{Z_{\sigma}}=\mathcal{O}(g^{2})$ and $\delta_{m_{\sigma}}=-g\hskip 0.5pt\hskip 0.5ptG^{\varphi}(1)-\frac{1}{2}g_{\sigma}\hskip 0.5pt\hskip 0.5ptG^{\sigma}(1)+\mathcal{O}(g^{2})$ . The same is true for the self-energy of $\varphi$ to first order, which is given by

