It is clear that the diagrams on the second line of (3.44) all cancel in our renormalization scheme, while the two diagrams associated with the $\mathcal{O}(g^{2})$ vertex counterterms can be absorbed into the $\mathcal{O}(g^{2})$ part of the $\delta_{m_{\sigma}}$ counterterm, as they yield just a constant factor $-\frac{1}{2}\delta_{g_{\sigma}}\hskip 0.5pt\hskip 0.5ptG^{\sigma}(1)-\frac{1}{2}\delta_{g}\hskip 0.5pt\hskip 0.5ptG^{\varphi}(1)$ . So, to $\mathcal{O}(g^{2})$ $\sigma$ ’s self-energy is given by the sum of sunset diagrams,

